course: dictionary
lesson: 1126
title: Words for big moments
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A breakthrough is an important discovery or step forward that suddenly solves a problem or makes great progress. The parts of the word give a clue: you break through something that was in your way.
explain: Read the context: «It was widely reported that scientists used AI to predict the shapes of proteins, a breakthrough that helps research into medicines.» The words helps research into medicines tell you this was a big step forward, not a small one.
explain: A breakthrough can also be the moment someone finally succeeds after trying for a long time. Sam practised fractions for weeks, then one day they clicked. That moment was a breakthrough. Words like major or medical before it show how big the step was.
fact: Breakthrough is a noun, so you can write a breakthrough or breakthroughs.
fact: A breakthrough is an important discovery or development that suddenly solves a problem.
fact: A breakthrough can also be a moment when someone finally succeeds after trying for a long time.
fact: Useful phrases: make a breakthrough, a major breakthrough, a medical breakthrough, breakthrough moment.
fact: Penicillin, vaccines and DNA are famous science breakthroughs.
exercise: «It was widely reported that scientists used AI to predict the shapes of proteins, a breakthrough that helps research into medicines.» What is a breakthrough here? | *An important discovery that makes great progress | A loud noise in a lab | A small, everyday chore | A type of pencil
exercise: Maya practised her times tables for months, then one day she got them all right. Which word fits this moment of finally succeeding? | A pause | A spelling error | *A breakthrough | A weather warning
exercise: Which phrase completes the sentence? «Scientists finally made ___ in finding a new treatment.» | a blackout | a backpack | *a breakthrough | a bedtime
test: In «The team made a breakthrough after weeks of trying», what does breakthrough mean? | A cold drink after training | *A moment of finally succeeding | A bad mistake | A long holiday trip
test: Which sentence uses breakthrough correctly? | We went to the breakthrough to buy shoes. | *The new medicine was a major breakthrough for doctors. | The breakthrough ate my lunch. | Breakthrough is a colour of paint.
exam: In «In a UKLO Breakthrough puzzle, you work out a language's rules from a few examples», what does Breakthrough mean? | *The first, easiest level of the UK Linguistics Olympiad | The final, hardest puzzle of the competition | A paper used for painting | A kind of football goal
